text.section:
The Board shall promulgate regulations to implement the provisions of this section that include:

Criteria for when the imposition of sanctions or initiation of court proceedings as specified in § 32.1-27, 32.1-27.1, or a combination thereof are appropriate in order to ensure prompt correction of violations involving noncompliance with requirements of any order of the Board or Commissioner or any provision of or regulation promulgated pursuant to Chapter 5 (§ 32.1-123 et seq.);


Criteria for the imposition of sanctions;


A schedule of civil penalties, which shall be uniform for each type of specific violation;


Procedures for the imposition of sanctions consistent with the Administrative Process Act (§ 2.2-4000 et seq.); and


Provisions for the prompt notification of the Department of Medical Assistance Services whenever any license is revoked or suspended for the purpose of terminating or suspending the applicable Medicaid provider agreement.
